## VERDICT: PASS

---

### Executive Summary

Phase 242 delivers portable governed-procedure execution evidence semantics: a deterministic evaluator, a published JSON Schema, and a semantics reference. The independent reviewer PASSed on the rebased head and confirmed the core threat model holds: an agent controlling only the evidence array cannot satisfy an independent-class requirement (observer required, observer must be a declared trusted principal, and an externally supplied VerifiedClaim must match the sha256 of the entire canonical claim; additionalProperties:false closes mutation paths). No fail-open path on the canonical route: missing evidence is unsatisfied, only status=completed is accepted, unknown classes are enum-rejected, and the contract fails unless every requirement is satisfied. Razor limits met; no unsafe constructs; only literal-path resource reads.

### Reviewer findings, both closed in this promotion

- F1 (schema/reference drift): the published schema admitted an independent-class requirement without trustedPrincipals -- the mandatory rule lived only in the Python cross-check, so a downstream schema-only validator got a weaker meaning than canonical Qor. Closed: the schema now carries the if/contains rule requiring non-empty trustedPrincipals when an independent class is accepted, with a schema-only rejection test (absent and empty both fail).
- F2 (unstated trust-domain assumption): requirements authorship decides what counts, so an actor authoring both requirements and evidence can accept agent-declared everywhere and satisfy the contract -- the same imitation threat routed through policy authorship. Closed: the reference now states the precondition (the requirements array MUST originate from a trust domain the evidence producer does not control; the evaluator enforces satisfaction over declared policy and cannot detect self-serving policy), with a test documenting the precondition boundary.
- Minor observations recorded, not acted on: unused CONTRACT_VERSION constant, double _candidate_reasons pass, per-call schema re-read, TypeError surface on canonical_claim_digest for non-JSON values. Curly quotes in the reference normalized to ASCII.

### Reviewer confirmations recorded

Reference-vs-implementation drift: none beyond F1 (exact procedure/subject binding, input digest, non-ordinal classes, completed-only, required-set completeness all enforced where declared). Tests: 16 delivered tests, 13 rejection/error paths, mapped 1:1 to the plan's declared behaviors; this promotion adds 2 (now 18/18). Phase 241 boundary coherence: no downstream hook can redefine class meaning or validity; no consequence authority returned. FEATURE_INDEX FX026 row cites real source and a real invoking test. SCHEMA_REGISTRY carries the schema with new-ceremony justification. Publication boundary clean.

